      "title": "Section B, Question 3",
      "prompt": {
        "en": "If we add all of its digits for a certain positive integer, we could get a new positive integer. This procedure could be repeated, until the final result has only one digit.\n\nFor example, 1234 would produce a new integer 10 (1+2+3+4), and finally 1 (1+0). Janet wants to write a program to input a 5-digit positive integer less than 32768, and output the final single digit after performing the above-mentioned procedure.\n\nHere is her code:\n\nHowever, she realizes that her program does not work for some cases. Help Janet write down in F a counter-example which is within the input range.\n\nScoring:\n2 marks if the written integer is a correct counter-example\n3 marks if the written counter-example is the maximum possible integer"
      },
      "points": 3,
      "blanks": [
        {
          "id": "F",
          "maxChars": 5
        }
